{#- The director's ordering of a sequential turn's primaries (FR-MULTI-6; #174).

Under ``sequence_order = director`` a turn with several primaries asks the narrator once who acts
first. The ``system`` block holds the rating guidance (always first, FR-RATE-4), the custom
instructions, the scenario text, the director's notes (the narrator's context alone, FR-SCN-11),
the scene, the last beats as the narrator perceives them (``think`` excluded), each primary's
public card, and the ordering contract. The ``user`` block is the player input. The answer is the
call's ``response_schema`` (``{order: [ids]}``): every primary, once. -#}
{% macro line(entry) -%}
{% if entry.text %}{{ entry.text }}{% else %}{{ entry.name }}:{% if entry.say %} "{{ entry.say }}"{% endif %}{% if entry.do %} *{{ entry.do }}*{% endif %}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
{% block system %}
{% if rating_guidance %}
## Content rating guidance
{{ rating_guidance }}

{% endif %}
{% if custom_instructions %}
## Custom instructions
{{ custom_instructions }}

{% endif %}
{% if scenario_text %}
{{ scenario_text }}

{% endif %}
{% if director_notes %}
{{ director_notes }}

{% endif %}
{% if scene %}
## Scene
{{ scene }}

{% endif %}
{% if working_memory %}
## What has happened
{% for beat in working_memory %}
- {{ beat }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
## Who acts first
You are the narrator. These characters each answer {{ player_input.name }} in this turn, one after another, each seeing what the ones before did:
{% for candidate in director_candidates %}
- {{ candidate.name }} (id {{ candidate.id }}){% if candidate.card %}: {{ candidate.card }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
Answer with `order`: every one of their ids, once each, in the order they should act.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
{{ player_input.name }}:{% if player_input.say %} "{{ player_input.say }}"{% endif %}{% if player_input.do %} *{{ player_input.do }}*{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
